Message-ID: <-zFx-jWJCpg.8q7nKg4Y7NQJ@corpling-with-r.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <-zFx-jWJCpg.NVykQ8SHngoJ@corpling-with-r.groups.google.com>
References: <-zFx-jWJCpg.NVykQ8SHngoJ@corpling-with-r.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/corpling-with-r/c/-zFx-jWJCpg/m/8q7nKg4Y7NQJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

How about

- in a first step, loading the file and pasting it all together:
corpus <- paste(scan("something.txt", what=character(0), sep="\n"),
collapse=" ")

- in a second step, replacing ellipses etc. by 'tags' like this
corpus <- gsub("\\.{3}", "_ELLIPSIS_", corpus, perl=T)
# similar replacements for other things

- in a third step, using this to get 'sentences':
sentences <- unlist(strsplit(corpus, "[\\.\\;\\:\\?\\!]", perl=T))

STG
--
Stefan Th. Gries
